From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Xe Chromium Patches <luke@agent54.org>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:18:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 20/50] direct route: close() and end of stream release everything at once

Blink: close() and end of stream (now the same) resolve a pending read with
null, make every later read() resolve null (no ready frame is handed out
after close), drop the renderer's references to every slot image not held
by a VideoFrame and stop the browser side. Frames still held stay valid
until they are closed; each then releases its slot, and the pipe closes
after the last one.

Browser: new GuestFrameTextureSourceHost.Stop(held, release tokens) and
ReleaseSlot(index, token). Stop cancels the source's copies in viz, ends the
keep-alive (capturer count) and the source's frame-rate requests, and drops
the images of slots not held (after the reader's release token; after the
pending copy if one is in flight). The images count against the quota until
dropped.

Viz: new FrameSinkManager.CancelKeyedCopyOutputRequests(frame_sink_id, key):
the sink drops queued and parked requests with that key (they complete with
an empty result) and forgets the key's damage count. The browser calls it on
Stop and when a source goes away.

Also fixes a lifetime bug the new test exposed: GuestFrameTextureSource is
now an ActiveScriptWrappable that stays alive while a read() is pending (it
could be collected with the read's resolver unresolved, a DCHECK), and it
closes when its context is destroyed.

Test: ControlledFrameTextureSourceTest.Quota also checks that read() after
close() is null, that a frame held across close() still has the guest's
pixels, and that after closing, the document can allocate the same amount
again.
---
diff --git a/chrome/browser/controlled_frame/controlled_frame_apitest.cc b/chrome/browser/controlled_frame/controlled_frame_apitest.cc
--- a/chrome/browser/controlled_frame/controlled_frame_apitest.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/controlled_frame/controlled_frame_apitest.cc
@@ -1105,6 +1105,41 @@
       }
       return 'never refused';
     })();)"));
+
+  // close() gives the memory back at once, except for frames still held,
+  // which stay valid until they are closed; read() after close() is null.
+  EXPECT_EQ("released", content::EvalJs(app_frame, R"(
+    (async () => {
+      const held = await sources[0].read();
+      for (const s of sources) s.close();
+      if ((await sources[1].read()) !== null) return 'frame after close';
+      const c = new OffscreenCanvas(4, 4);
+      const ctx = c.getContext('2d');
+      ctx.drawImage(held, 0, 0, 4, 4);
+      const d = ctx.getImageData(2, 2, 1, 1).data;
+      if (!(d[0] < 60 && d[1] > 180 && d[2] < 60)) return 'held frame ' + d;
+      held.close();
+      const f = document.querySelector('controlledframe');
+      for (let i = 0; i < 8; i++) {
+        let ok = false;
+        // Stop() and the next CreateSource() travel on different pipes.
+        for (let t = 0; t < 20 && !ok; t++) {
+          const s = await f.createTextureSource(
+              {width: 1920, height: 1080, poolSize: 16});
+          const vf = await s.read();
+          if (vf) {
+            vf.close();
+            sources[i] = s;
+            ok = true;
+          } else {
+            await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, 100));
+          }
+        }
+        if (!ok) return 'not released at ' + i;
+      }
+      for (const s of sources) s.close();
+      return 'released';
+    })();)"));
 }
 
